cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the papers whose methods you use."
title: "ssiv: shift-share (Bartik) instrumental variables in Python"
abstract: >-
  ssiv implements estimation and inference for shift-share (Bartik) instrumental
  variable designs in Python: OLS and IV regressions with exposure-robust AKM and
  AKM0 confidence intervals (Adão, Kolesár and Morales, 2019), Rotemberg weights
  (Goldsmith-Pinkham, Sorkin and Swift, 2020) and shock-level estimation (Borusyak,
  Hull and Jaravel, 2022). Results are validated against the published output of the
  R package ShiftShareSE on the Autor, Dorn and Hanson (2013) data.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Iskakov
    given-names: Serik
version: 0.1.2
date-released: 2026-11-17
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/iskakovs/ssiv"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/ssiv/"
keywords:
